1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,645
Why didn't Ravan lay a hand on Sita in Lanka?

2
00:00:03,645 --> 00:00:05,695
Was it out of righteousness?

3
00:00:05,695 --> 00:00:07,160
Many people believe,

4
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:09,639
no matter how evil Ravan was,

5
00:00:09,639 --> 00:00:11,242
he still knew his limits.

6
00:00:11,242 --> 00:00:12,460
He did abduct Sita,

7
00:00:14,570 --> 00:00:17,476
yet never even laid a finger on her. Then,

8
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:18,998
bringing her to Lanka,

9
00:00:18,998 --> 00:00:21,350
he gave Sita a one-year ultimatum.

10
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,761
[Ravan] You have twelve months, Maithili.

11
00:00:23,761 --> 00:00:24,659
Refuse me still,

12
00:00:24,659 --> 00:00:26,230
and you will lose your life.

13
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,974
Sita wouldn't even speak directly to him.

14
00:00:28,974 --> 00:00:31,073
Placing a blade of grass between them,

15
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:31,570
she said—

16
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:34,784
[Sita] Lord Ram hasn't given me leave,

17
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:38,310
or the fire of my devotion would burn you to ashes this instant.

18
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:40,857
Then,

19
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:43,634
as Ram's army reached the ocean's shore,

20
00:00:43,634 --> 00:00:46,480
in Lanka's council, Mahaparshva spoke up—

21
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:50,140
[Mahaparshva] My King! What you desire,

22
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:51,130
take it by force.

23
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,770
That was when Ravan revealed a terrifying secret—

24
00:00:57,510 --> 00:00:59,460
[Ravan] Mahaparshva! Long ago,

25
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,320
I forced myself upon the nymph Punjiksthala.

26
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,790
[Ravan] Then Brahma laid a curse on me—

27
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:09,482
[Brahma] Force yourself on any woman ever again,

28
00:01:09,482 --> 00:01:12,190
and your head will shatter into a hundred pieces!

29
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:14,669
[Ravan] Terrified of that curse,

30
00:01:14,669 --> 00:01:16,580
I dare not lay a hand on Sita.

31
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:23,440
So it wasn't righteousness that stayed Ravan's hand; it was purely the dread of his own doom.

32
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:26,132
The true virtue was Sita's.

33
00:01:26,132 --> 00:01:28,808
She held the power to reduce Ravan to ashes,

34
00:01:28,808 --> 00:01:30,450
yet she restrained herself.

35
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:34,250
Holding back out of fear is not righteousness;

36
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:36,603
holding back when you hold the power...

37
00:01:36,603 --> 00:01:37,840
that is righteousness.

38
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,644
For more such secrets of Ravan,

39
00:01:40,644 --> 00:01:42,573
stay tuned for upcoming tales.

40
00:01:42,573 --> 00:01:44,760
Follow or subscribe to Naad Katha.

